{title: Heals the Brokenhearted}
{subtitle: Psalms 147:3}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb/D] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bb/D] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Praise the LORD [Bb/D]with a joyful [Eb]song
[Bb]It is good [Bb/D]to sing to our [Eb]God
How [Gm7]pleasant it is
How [F/A]fitting to praise him
The [Eb]LORD rebuilds Jerusalem
He gathers the outcasts of Israel
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Bb]heals the brokenheart[Eb]ed
And [Gm7]binds up [F]their [Eb]wounds
He [Bb]heals the bro[Bb/D]kenheart[Eb]ed
And [Gm7]binds [F]up their [Bb]wounds [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]He counts the num[Bb/D]ber of the [Eb]stars
[Bb]And calls [Bb/D]each one by name [Eb]
[Gm7]Great is our Lord
[F/A]Mighty in power
His [Eb]understanding has no limit
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Bb]heals the bro[Bb/D]kenheart[Eb]ed
[Gm7]And binds [F]up their [Eb]wounds
He [Bb]heals the bro[Bb/D]kenheart[Eb]ed
[Gm7]And binds [F]up their [Bb]wounds
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm7]The LORD lifts up the [Eb]humble
He casts the wicked to the [Gm7]ground
His power is end[Eb]less
His love is [F]deep
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He [Bb]heals the bro[Bb/D]kenheart[Eb]ed
And [Gm7]binds up [F]their [Eb]wounds
